The Role: Designer &nbsp;

As a Designer within our DCO team (Dynamic Creative Optimization), you will play a key role in shaping and evolving programmatic and social campaign creative on behalf of our ad-creative customers.&nbsp; This role requires exceptional art direction skills and a strong command of design industry standard software. Particularly in shaping existing and supplied campaigns into multiple touchpoints.  
&nbsp;
You’ll develop briefs into strategic solutions that capture attention, understand how to evolve creative executions for a diverse set of placements and formats, be able to think social-first and have the ability to generate new concepts and campaigns when required.   

With a strong understanding of commercial advertising and branding you will confidently present ideas and solutions to key stakeholders, pushing the bar for art direction and design systems in the DCO team’s process.

As part of our DCO team, you’ll also be positioned within Genius Sports Creative, our internal agency, meaning you may also have exposure to briefs from our Brand, Marketing and Broadcast creative teams. &nbsp;

Key Responsibilities    &nbsp;

• Act as a champion and guardian of clients’ brand identities, ensuring consistency and creative excellence.    &nbsp;

• Develop high-level creative concepts with minimal oversight, bringing fresh, unexpected ideas to the table.    &nbsp;

• Lead the development of concept-driven campaigns and scalable design systems.    &nbsp;

• Define forward-thinking art direction solutions that guide image-making, and content ecosystems across multiple platforms.    &nbsp;

• Translate strategic narratives into distinctive, ownable visual executions that flex across diverse digital placements.    &nbsp;

• Establish clear visual territories through mood systems, reference frameworks, compositional principles, and narrative guidelines.    &nbsp;

• Collaborate across disciplines including strategy, copywriting, motion, and technology to build complete performance based campaigns.    &nbsp;

• Balance multiple projects and clients, delivering compelling creative solutions on tight deadlines.    &nbsp;

• Produce inspiring and provocative work that connects and engages audiences.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Leverage AI-powered content creation tools to concept, visualize, and prototype design solutions.   
&nbsp;

